# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# This file is deliberately short. The only value the build needs is the API
# origin, and it is build-time configuration: there is no runtime config
# endpoint, no user-supplied base URL, and nothing that a hostile bundle could
# repoint.

# The exact origin of the backend. Must be https in production, must be an
# exact origin with no path and no trailing slash.
#
# This value ends up in exactly two places, and both matter:
#   - `connect-src` in the Content-Security-Policy, which is what makes a
#     static host safe to type a Microsoft password into. It must name this
#     origin and nothing else.
#   - the request target of every call in src/lib/api.ts, including the
#     credential POST.
VITE_API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
